# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This repo is a workspace: other repositories are cloned alongside it and
# worked on concurrently. None of them belong in this repo's history.
#
# The root is therefore an allowlist, everything is ignored unless named
# below. A repo cloned into the root is ignored the moment it appears, with no
# .gitignore edit and nothing to remember. `make lint` fails if a nested repo
# is ever tracked anyway, so the two mechanisms cover each other.
#
# Adding a new tracked file at the root means adding it here.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/*
!/.devcontainer/
!/.github/
!/.vscode/
!/docs/
!/.gitignore
!/.pymarkdown.json
!/CLAUDE.md
!/Makefile
!/README.md
!/LICENSE
!/shell.env.example
!/devcontainer-environment-variables.json.example
# The folder is tracked so it exists in a fresh clone; what you clone into
# it is not. VS Code still finds those repositories, because its scan walks
# directories rather than consulting .gitignore.
!/repos/
/repos/*
!/repos/.gitkeep

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-developer identity and secrets. The .example files above are committed;
# these are generated from them and reach the remote container only through
# Parameter Store. Listed explicitly so they stay ignored even if the
# allowlist above is edited.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/shell.env
/devcontainer-environment-variables.json
.devcontainer/aws-profile-map.json
.devcontainer/ssh-private-key
.claude/settings.local.json
